{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Adding your own functionality}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Adding_your_own_functionality}
\pard \fs36\cf1 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Macro Editor}
Adding your own functionality
\par \plain\fs24 
\par You may add your own functionality by executing programs you have written yourself, either in Visual C++ or in Visual Basic.
\par 
\par Use  the \ul Execute Program\plain\fs24 {\v 1KGATAT} instruction to call your program.
\par 
\par You may pass arguments in the command line.
\par 
\par Those who have access to the LEOAPI may obtain (or set) values of parameters such as the \ul Flag Variables\plain\fs24 {\v Flag_Variables__Semaphores_} to communicate with the program.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Allowing user response in macro}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Allowing_user_response_in_macro}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Adding your own functionality}
\fs36\cf1 Allowing user response in macro
\par \plain\fs24 If you need to get a response from the user to determine the execution sequence to be followed use the following technique
\par 
\par 
\par \ul YesNo Message\plain\fs24 {\v Message}: Flag 2 :Do you want to continue?
\par If  : \ul Flag 2\plain\fs24 {\v Flag_Variables__Semaphores_} = 0     Is True
\par \ul End The Macro\plain\fs24 {\v End_The_Macro}
\par EndIf Statement
\par continue execution from here.....
\par \page
