{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Attaching macros to keys}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Attaching_macros_to_keys}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Annotation Text}
\fs36 Attaching macros to keys\fs24 
\par Macros may be attached to \ul Special Function Keys\plain\fs24 {\v Special_Function_Keys}
\par 
\par This is achieved by naming the macro with the key name,
\par e.g. name the macro \b F5 \plain\fs24 or \b Shift F5 \plain\fs24 (Note only a single space between \b shift\plain\fs24  and the key name)
\par 
\par Note that if there is not a macro for the key in the library a \b Beep\plain\fs24  is sounded when the key is pressed.
\par 
\par Note also that the macro may not be initiated again until it has completed, attempting to do so will result in a \b Beep\plain\fs24 
\par \pard 
\par See also \ul Common Macros\plain\fs24 {\v Common_Macros}
\par \page
