{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Customising the Hard Panel}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Customising_the_Hard_Panel}
\pard \fs36\cf1 Customising the Hard Panel
\par \plain\fs24 If your SEM is fitted with a Hard Panel (Mark 2) it may be configured for your use.
\par [Applies to Leo 1500 only]
\par This is achieved by two facilities.
\par 
\par \b Hard Panel Buttons.\plain\fs24 
\par When one of the buttons on the Hard Panel is pressed (excluding the Stage axis control buttons) an associated macro is executed.
\par Pressing \b Button M1\plain\fs24  executes the Macro \b M1, \plain\fs24 pressing\b  Button M2\plain\fs24  executes the Macro \b M2,\plain\fs24  \b  \plain\fs24 pressing\b  Button M3\plain\fs24  executes the Macro \b M3\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard Default versions of these macros are supplied in the ...\'5cLEO32\'5cDISTRIB .directory. See \ul Search order\plain\fs24 {\v Search_Order_for_macro_execution} on how to override these macros
\par 
\par \b Knob Assignment\plain\fs24 
\par There is a macro Instruction \ul Knob\plain\fs24 {\v Knob} which is used to disable or assign a parameter to a knob.
\par 
\par Macros may therefore be constructed which assign complementary functions to the Hard Panel Knobs and to the Mouse.
\par These macros may be called from Toolbar Icons (Use \uldb Toolbar Editor\plain\fs24 {\v Contents@tooledit.hlp}), \ul Special function keys\plain\fs24 {\v Attaching_macros_to_keys}, or Hard Panel Buttons
\par \pard 
\par 
\par \page
