{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Editor Window}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Editor_Window}
\pard \fs36 Editor Window
\par \fs24 The editor window is used to edit and debug the currently displayed macro.
\par The macro name and version are displayed at the start of the macro in green.
\par Double clicking on the name/version will perform the \ul rename\plain\fs24 {\v Rename_macro} function.
\par 
\par Each macro\ul  instruction\plain\fs24 {\v Macro_Instructions} occupies one line
\par 
\par The selected (highlighted) instruction indicates the insertion point and Program Counter
\par Clicking on an instruction will select it.
\par 
\par Double clicking on an instruction will enable editing of the instruction.
\par \pard 
\par Inserting a new instruction will cause the instruction to be inserted AFTER the selected instruction and the new instruction will be selected as insertion point. If no instruction is selected insertion will be at the end of the macro.
\par 
\par The macro may be executed using \ul Run or F5\plain\fs24 {\v Run}, stopped by pressing \ul ESC\plain\fs24 {\v Stop}
\par Execution may be continued by pressing \ul F7\plain\fs24 {\v Continue}
\par For debugging you may \ul step (F10)\plain\fs24 {\v Step} through the macro.
\par 
\par Progress of the macro is indicated by the \ul Status Bar\plain\fs24 {\v Editor_Status_Bar}.
\par \pard 
\par \page
