{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Macro Library}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Macro_Library}
\pard \f1\fs36 Macro Library
\par \fs24 A Macro Library is a collection of macros held in memory ready for execution.
\par The macro library is loaded from a library file (.MLL) in the User Directory.
\par 
\par When macros are deleted or saved in memory the Library file is also updated.
\par 
\par If the User Directory is changed the Macro Library is loaded from the File in the new User D|irectory and any currently executing macros are terminated.
\par 
\par If the User Directory does not contain a macro library file then a new one is created (CURRENT.MLL) from a Standard Macro Library in ..\'5cLeo32\'5cDistrib\'5cDefault.MLL
\par \pard 
\par The Standard Macro Library contains all the Standard Macros required,  for the Standard Toolbar etc.
\par 
\par All macro libraries must contain these standard macros. This may be achieved either by Loading the Standard Library (Library-Load Standard Library) or by merging the Standard Library with the current Library (Library-Merge Standard Library)
\par \page
