{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Search Order for macro execution}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Search_Order_for_macro_execution}
\pard \fs36\cf1 Search Order for macro execution
\par \plain\fs24 When a macro is requested for execution the Macro Engine first tries to locate the macro in the current macro Library.
\par 
\par If the macro is not found in the libary it will try to execute it as a macro file MacroName.MLF in the current User Directory.
\par 
\par If this also fails it will then try to execute a macro file  ...\'5cLEO32\'5cUser\'5cMacroName.MLF
\par 
\par If this also fails it will try to execute a macro file  ...\'5cLEO32\'5cDistrib\'5cMacroName.MLF.
\par 
\par A number of standard macros are located in the Distribution directory.
\par \pard To override them create new macros in the macro library or macro files in the \'5cUSER directory.
\par 
\par See \uldb \b Customising Default Files\plain\b\fs24 {\v Customising_default_files}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Macro Locations\plain\b\fs24 {\v Macro_Locations}\plain\fs24 
