{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Standard Conditions}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Standard_Conditions}
\pard \fs36\cf1 Standard Conditions
\par \plain\fs24 This function is executed on request from the User Interface or if \ul Restore Conditions\plain\fs24 {\v Restore_Conditions} fails.
\par 
\par The action is as follows
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par 1. Execute the macro STANDARD if it exists in the current macro library. 
\par 2. Otherwise load and execute the file STANDARD.MLC if it exists in the User Directory.
\par 3. Otherwise load and execute the file ..\'5cLEO32\'5cUSER\'5cSTANDARD.MLC if it exists
\par 4. Otherwise load and execute the file ..\'5cLEO32\'5cDISTRIB\'5cSTANDARD.MLC.
\par 
\par The default behaviour is therefore to execute the file in the Distribution directory (case 4).
\par 
\par An alternative file may be created and placed in \'5cLEO32\'5cUSER this will therefore be executed when any new user directory is created and conditions restored (case 3)
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par NOTE: The macro in file STANDARD.MLC must be named \b Standard\plain\fs24 
\par \page
