{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Wait For State}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Wait_For_State}
\pard \fs36\cf1 Macro Instruction:Wait For State
\par \plain\f4\fs24 This instruction waits for the specified digital parameter to be the defined state or until the timeout period expires. 
\par 
\par Steps to the next instruction when the required state is achieved.
\par 
\par If the instruction times out the macro stops with an error state (default action) or optionally continues with the next instruction.
\par 
\par The option to continue on timeout is provided so that alternative action may be taken on timeout (e.g. an IF statement following the waitfor can check if the condition has not been met)
\par \pard 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Wait For dialog}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} GEDWQ}
\pard \f1\fs36 Wait For dialog\fs24 
\par This dialog is used to define a \ul Wait For instruction\plain\fs24 {\v Wait_For_State}
\par 
\par Select the required parameter from the drop down list.
\par 
\par The lower drop down list displays the possible state values for the parameter.
\par 
\par If this is a new instruction the current state value will be displayed, if editing an existing instruction the state value will be that previously defined.
\par 
\par A timeout value (in seconds) defines how long the instruction will wait.
\par 
\par There is a checkbox which defines the action on Timeout. If you wish the macro to halt on timeout (the default action) then check the box.
\par \pard If you uncheck the box the next instruction in sequence will be executed.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} While}
