{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Instruction Timeout}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1280J7M}
\pard \fs36\cf1 Instruction Timeout
\par \plain\fs24 If an attempt is made to set a \uldb digital parameter\plain\fs24 {\v Set_Digital_State}, set an \uldb Analogue parameter \plain\fs24 {\v Set_Analogue_Parameter}or execute a \uldb command\plain\fs24 {\v Execute_Command} which is disabled then the instruction is repeatedly executed without stepping on to the next instruction.
\par 
\par If after a timeout period the instruction still cannot proceed a message box is displayed notifying the user.
\par 
\par The user may choose:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab To stop the Macro
\par \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab To skip the instruction
\par \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab To wait a further timeout period
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The default timeout period is 10 seconds.
\par \pard\tx355 The period may be changed from the menu using \b Edit - timeout\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Customising default files}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Customising_default_files}
\pard\keepn \fs36\cf1 Customising default files
\par \pard \plain\fs24 There are default files installed during Leo-32 installation, these are found in the ...\'5cLEO32\'5cDISTRIB directory.
\par 
\par These files provide default behaviour and may be modified as required and installed in your own user directory (hence only apply when the specific user directory is in use) or \uldb \b saved\plain\b\fs24 {\v SaveAs_Common}\plain\fs24  as\b  \uldb common files\plain\b\fs24 {\v Common_Macros}\plain\fs24  (hence will apply to all users). (see \uldb \b Search Order\plain\b\fs24 {\v Search_Order_for_macro_execution}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b Macro Locations\plain\b\fs24 {\v Macro_Locations}\plain\fs24 )
\par 
\par These files are:
\par 
\par \b Standard.MLC\plain\fs24 
\par \pard Sets standard conditions, see \uldb Standard\plain\fs24 {\v Standard_Conditions}
\par 
\par \b Specimen Change.MLF\plain\fs24  (Leo 1500 only)
\par Executed from Specimen Exchange button on Airlock Panel.
\par See comments in macro and \uldb How To\plain\fs24 {\v Contents@how_to.hlp} : automating specimen exchange
\par 
\par \b Video Print\plain\fs24 
\par Executed when Video Printer is selected as output device.
\par Provides an \uldb \b uncluttered image\plain\b\fs24 {\v Uncluttered_image_for_video_printing}\plain\fs24  for 15 seconds to permit the user to make a video print.
\par 
\par \b Resume Exchange.MLF\plain\fs24  (Leo 1500 only)
\par Executed from Resume Exchange button on Airlock Panel.
\par \pard See comments in macro and \uldb How To\plain\fs24 {\v Contents@how_to.hlp} : automating specimen exchange
\par 
\par \b HV_DETECTOR.MLF\plain\fs24  (Leo 435VP and 438VP only)
\par Detector selection.
\par Executed when switching into HV mode. Not used if VPSE Detector fitted.
\par 
\par \b VP_DETECTOR.MLF\plain\fs24  (Leo 435VP and 438VP only)
\par Detector selection.
\par Executed when switching into VP mode. Not used if VPSE Detector fitted.
\par 
\par \b Mouse Stigmation.MLF\plain\fs24 
\par Executed when the Stigmation button on the \uldb SEM Control Apertures\plain\fs24 {\v 295DOW3@tabmgr.hlp} tab is pressed.
\par \pard By default selects the \b Stigmation X and Y\plain\fs24  parameters to the Left Mouse button for two dimensional adjustment.
\par Alternatively may select the \b Stig X Only\plain\fs24  and \b Stig Y only\plain\fs24  parameters to the left and middle buttonsa repectively to permit individual adjustment.
\par 
\par \b Mouse Aperture Align.MLF \plain\fs24 (Leo 1500 only)
\par Executed when the Aperture Align button on the \uldb SEM Control Apertures\plain\fs24 {\v 295DOW3@tabmgr.hlp} tab is pressed.
\par By default selects the \b Aperture Align X and Y\plain\fs24  parameters to the Left Mouse button for two dimensional adjustment.
\par \pard Alternatively may select the \b Aper Align X Only\plain\fs24  and \b Aper Align Y only\plain\fs24  parameters to the left and middle buttonsa repectively to permit individual adjustment.
\par 
\par \b Toolbar\plain\fs24 
\par In addition many of the toolbar icons call macros, or they may be modified to call macros. These macros may also be saved in your own macro library or saved as common macros. See \uldb \b Standard Toolbar functions\plain\b\fs24 {\v 4AX50PD@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24  and \uldb \b toolbar editor\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents@tooledit.hlp}
\par 
\par 
\par \pard See Also
\par \uldb Macro - contents\plain\b\fs24 {\v Contents}
\par \uldb Macro - Overview\plain\b\fs24 {\v Macros___Overview}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
